warning[SCXML060]: `+` adds numbers in XPath, so adding the string 'Hello, ' yields `NaN`
 --> tests/ui/scxml060-xpath-string-addition.scx:5:45
  |
5 |       <log label="greeting" expr="'Hello, ' + $name + '!'"/>
  |                                   ----------------------- this sum is `NaN`
  |                                             ^ numeric addition, not string concatenation
  |
  = note: XPath converts both operands of `+` to numbers; a string that is not a number converts to `NaN`, and `NaN` plus anything is `NaN`
  = help: join strings with `concat()`: `concat('Hello, ', $name, '!')`
  = spec: SCXML CR 2014 §C.3 The XPath Data Model
  = spec: XPath 1.0 §3.5 Numbers
help: join the strings with `concat()`
  |
5 |       <log label="greeting" expr="concat('Hello, ', $name, '!')"/>
  |                                   ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

